e",[53,223,225],{"id":224},"week-4-taking-the-project-from-it-works-to-ready-to-ship","Week 4: Taking the project from \"it works\" to \"ready to ship\"",[58,227,228,235,242,249,256,263,270],{},[61,229,230],{},[64,231,234],{"href":232,"rel":233},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F05\u002Fclaude-code-hooks-auto-format\u002F",[68],"Day 22: Hooks — Claude Code's Lifecycle Triggers",[61,236,237],{},[64,238,241],{"href":239,"rel":240},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F06\u002Fclaude-code-vitest-unit-tests\u002F",[68],"Day 23: Tests as Your Safety Net — Unit Testing with Vitest",[61,243,244],{},[64,245,248],{"href":246,"rel":247},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F07\u002Frefactor-ai-generated-code\u002F",[68],"Day 24: Refactoring to Pay Down Tech Debt",[61,250,251],{},[64,252,255],{"href":253,"rel":254},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F08\u002Fdeploy-vite-app-to-github-pages\u002F",[68],"Day 25: Going Live — Deploying to GitHub Pages",[61,257,258],{},[64,259,262],{"href":260,"rel":261},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F09\u002Fclaude-code-add-feature-after-launch\u002F",[68],"Day 26: Your First Update After Launch",[61,264,265],{},[64,266,269],{"href":267,"rel":268},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F10\u002Fgithub-pull-request-coderabbit-ai-code-review\u002F",[68],"Day 27: Pull Requests and Automatic Code Review with CodeRabbit",[61,271,272],{},[64,273,276],{"href":274,"rel":275},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F11\u002Fclaude-code-save-token-cost\u002F",[68],"Day 28: Week 4 Wrap-Up — How to Save Tokens in Claude Code",[53,278,280],{"id":279},"the-last-two-days","The last two days",[58,282,283,290],{},[61,284,285],{},[64,286,289],{"href":287,"rel":288},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F12\u002Fvibe-coding-workflow-sop\u002F",[68],"Day 29: My Vibe Coding Workflow SOP",[61,291,292],{},[64,293,296],{"href":294,"rel":295},"https:\u002F\u002Fisraynotarray.com\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F13\u002Fvibe-coding-30-days-recap\u002F",[68],"Day 30: Series Recap and the Full Table of Contents",[19,298,300],{"id":299},"wrapping-up","Wrapping up",[12,302,303],{},"That's about it. 30 days, and we're done.",[12,305,306],{},"To sum it all up:",[58,308,309,312,315],{},[61,310,311],{},"A tiny app and a big project share the same skeleton: a spec, tests, reviews, and automated deployment.",[61,313,314],{},"Tools will keep changing, but describing, verifying, and breaking things down won't.",[61,316,317],{},"Your next step is to start a project of your own.",[12,319,320],{},"Thank you to everyone who made it this far, whether you built along every single day or just followed the story all the way to the finish line.",[12,322,323],{},"I'll keep writing about new pitfalls and new toys as standalone posts here on the blog.",[12,325,326],{},"I hope these 30 days helped you actually step into the world of Vibe Coding. That's a wrap, see you in the next series!",{"title":328,"searchDepth":329,"depth":329,"links":330},"",2,[331,332,333,341],{"id":21,"depth":329,"text":22},{"id":31,"depth":329,"text":32},{"id":47,"depth":329,"text":48,"children":334},[335,337,338,339,340],{"id":55,"depth":336,"text":56},3,{"id":114,"depth":336,"text":115},{"id":169,"depth":336,"text":170},{"id":224,"depth":336,"text":225},{"id":279,"depth":336,"text":280},{"id":299,"depth":329,"text":300},"AI","2026-10-13 09:00:00","The finale of 30 Days of Vibe Coding: a few honest thoughts on finishing, plus the full table of contents for all 30 days, grouped by week.","md","en",{},true,"\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002Fvibe-coding-30-days-recap","3",{"title":6,"description":344},false,"en\u002FAI\u002Fvibe-coding-30-days-recap",[355,356,357,358,359,360,361],"Vibe Coding","Vibe Coding Lessons","Claude Code 30 Days","iThome Ironman","Vibe Coding Series Index","Claude Code","30 Days of Vibe Coding","\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F13\u002Fvibe-coding-30-days-recap\u002F","-Sh0OwRpN-ZA0pl6gpjGdQ_mJwJrMTYdIbMT6YWrdCU",{"newer":7,"older":365},{"url":366,"title":367,"date":368},"\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F12\u002Fvibe-coding-workflow-sop\u002F","30 Days of Vibe Coding | Day 29: My Vibe Coding Workflow SOP","2026-10-12 09:00:00",[370,372,377],{"url":366,"title":367,"date":368,"readingMinutes":371},"13",{"url":373,"title":374,"date":375,"readingMinutes":376},"\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F11\u002Fclaude-code-save-token-cost\u002F","30 Days of Vibe Coding | Day 28: Week 4 Wrap-Up — How to Save Tokens in Claude Code","2026-10-11 09:00:00","5",{"url":378,"title":379,"date":380,"readingMinutes":381},"\u002Fen\u002Fai\u002F2026\u002F10\u002F10\u002Fgithub-pull-request-coderabbit-ai-code-review\u002F","30 Days of Vibe Coding | Day 27: Pull Requests and Automatic Code Review with CodeRabbit","2026-10-10 09:00:00","8",1791821156127]